    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain unobstructed could significantly improve response times and apparatus maneuvering, particularly for larger emergency vehicles. Keeping the driveway clear of parked vehicles and maintaining adequate vertical clearance along the approach would support efficient access to both the main building and detached structure. Clearly marking the primary access point from the street frontage may assist responding units in locating the entry during low-visibility or nighttime conditions. Given the limited rear access, identifying and communicating an interior staging area to local responders in advance could facilitate more effective operations across the property."
