    "recommendations": "Reducing the concentration of brush and managing the continuous grass and heavy ground vegetation in the area surrounding the structure could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity near the building. Thinning or removing shrubs closest to the structure and creating separation between remaining vegetation and the building perimeter may reduce direct fuel exposure to the structure. Where scattered trees are present near improvements, removing low-hanging limbs and reducing understory vegetation beneath the canopy could help limit vertical fuel continuity. Given that a single access route serves the property, keeping that route clear of encroaching vegetation along its margins would support firefighter access and improve conditions for both suppression operations and evacuation. Maintaining a well-managed buffer of reduced fuel immediately surrounding the structure, and where feasible expanding that buffer outward through the surrounding brushland, could further improve overall wildfire resilience and property preparedness."
